# Approved visual baselines are committed; candidate and diff images are not.
**/*-actual.png
**/*-diff.png
**/__screenshots__/**/*.actual.png

# ─── Benchmark and research output ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Reports are published deliberately, not swept in by `git add`.
benchmark/results/
benchmark/.cache/
benchmark/corpus/.fetched/

# Python suites (the optical one, and any that follow) sit outside the pnpm
# workspace deliberately. Written generically rather than per suite: the first
# of these was kept out of the repository only by a .gitignore that `uv` writes
# inside the virtualenv, which is 500 MB of protection resting on one tool's
# internal behaviour. Nothing a run produces is committed: venvs, rendered
# samples, model caches, per-cell JSON and the written tables are all derivable.
# What a run changed in the design graduates into docs/decisions.md instead.
benchmark/**/results/*.json
benchmark/**/results/*.md
benchmark/**/samples/
benchmark/**/page/
benchmark/**/models/

# Research prose is local working material and is not published under the
# project's name: machine-assisted syntheses of other people's work, only spot
# checked, and candid about competitors and legal exposure. A finding graduates
# into docs/decisions.md citing the primary source; the review itself stays out.
research/
*.bench.json
!benchmark/results/**/*.published.json

